Z||000001||stsmithgt||10-23-2000||05:35 PM||||Nice looking wheel.  Better keep an eye on it.  Some guys might want it more than you.  Just kidding T.G.O.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  I prefer an after market wheel too.  I don't have any pics though.  I think I'm getting closer to buying a digital camera due to this no pics frustration.<P>I found a picture of it. this should take you their if you want a look.<BR>Oops not so easy.<BR>bottom of the page has a "find" catagory.  Look under signature series. the page will show up.  Scroll down to part#  1031<BR>It's a similar design.  Mines the red "D"shaped Corsa model.<BR><A HREF="http://www.grantproducts.com/idea.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.grantproducts.com/idea.html</A> <P><p>[This message has been edited by stsmithgt (edited 10-23-2000).]||||reg||14
Z||000002||BAM-BAM||10-23-2000||06:54 PM||||  STS, that's the Grant wheel I refered to once before. It lists for $275.00 and is 50% vynal. The MOMO I bought (same design) is 100% leather and I payed $219.00. Not to bad of a deal as far as I am concerned. <P> Later,BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach Springs/KYB shocks and struts<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats, Carpet and headliner! YEAH BABY-YEAH||||reg||1
Z||000003||stsmithgt||10-24-2000||10:22 AM||||I didn't even ask if it was all leather or not.  I liked it, so I bought it.  Simple logic.  If there is vinyl on this wheel, it must be on the inner part where the wear is minimal.  Works for me.  I was looking for a MOMO when I ran across this one and the gooo coming out of my original one had to go, fast.  I spent about $200.00 for the wheel plus about $25.00 for the adapter at Tognotti's Auto World in Sacramento.  You'll like you new wheel better than the original.  And to think your car will be MORE enjoyable to drive. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
